sm-elite (0.2.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * List nodes with public nodes first, then private nodes (below 2000),
    each in numeric order, in the node buttons, groups, the Local node menu,
    and the node cards.
  * Schedule: weekly connect, monitor, disconnect, saved sound, or
    commands.ini actions at a set time, run as the user who added them.
  * Action log for admins under System: control actions, announcements,
    access list and DVSwitch changes, schedules, file edits, restarts,
    users, and logins, kept for 90 days.
  * Admin config editor also edits asdb.txt (names apply on save) and
    node_info.ini (the status updater runs on save), with backups.

 -- Jory A. Pratt <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 18:40:00 -0600

sm-elite (0.2.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship supermon-ng's node status updater as
    /usr/lib/sm-elite/ast_node_status_update.py with sm-elite-node-status.timer
    (every 4 minutes), so the node status block keeps working without
    supermon-ng. It stands aside while supermon-ng's own timer is enabled.
  * Install writes /etc/sm-elite/node_info.ini, copied from supermon-ng when
    present or built from rpt.conf.
  * Depend on python3-requests; suggest saytime-weather-rb and skywarnplus-ng.

 -- Jory A. Pratt <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 18:45:00 -0600

sm-elite (0.2.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a blank dashboard when the favorites file is missing: the live node
    feed starts first, and the Favorites panel explains the problem.
  * Favorites from Supermon are copied into /etc/sm-elite at install, so
    removing supermon-ng no longer takes them away.
  * Upgrades repair a config whose favorites folder no longer exists.

